-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against a 61,198-frame
              recording; Tang FPGA board: loads with DivMMC automap on and
              runs to the game's menu (the board's key input did not reach the
              menu). Played by the owner on a ZX Spectrum Next (KS3),
              2026-11-27: broken: once a game starts, the line of text under
              the play area is corrupted (being looked at).

  Replay      IDENTICAL on a 61,198-frame recording through 157 rooms: at
              every hook and every attribute painter call original and patched
              code compared from the same state (every register but R, all 48K
              RAM), every figure's pixels against its sprites after each draw
              (13.7 million pixels); 424 unit cases; 9 deliberately broken
              builds rejected

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: played by
              the owner, broken: once a game starts, the line of text under
              the play area is corrupted (being looked at)

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
